1
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:08,890
Excuse me. Can you help me?

2
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,700
Sure, what do you want?

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,180
Where is 83 Wooster Street?

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:16,550
That's easy. Walk to the corner.

5
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,510
Then make a left turn.

6
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:21,530
Then walk two blocks to the traffic light.

7
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:23,150
Make another left to Wooster.

8
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:24,870
Thank you.

9
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:26,800
To the corner and then a left?

10
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,160
Yeah. A left.

11
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,980
Hot dog? Only seventy-five cents.

12
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:44,580
No. Thank you. I have a dinner date.

13
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:59,180
555-9470...and it's busy....

14
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:10,130
Try again.

15
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:21,090
555-9470...and it's still busy.

16
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,280
Excuse me, ma'am.

17
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:25,780
I'm looking for 83 Wooster Street.

18
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:28,800
Yes. Wooster Street is two blocks,

19
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:35,280
and 83 is to the right, about two houses.

20
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,960
Thank you, thank you!

21
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:47,930
You're welcome.

22
00:01:47,930 --> 00:01:49,510
Who is it?

23
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:51,290
Harry Bennett. Is this Susan?

24
00:01:51,290 --> 00:01:52,820
Yes, it is. Come up.

25
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:55,440
I'm on the top floor.

26
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:58,460
Hello, Harry. It's nice to meet you.

27
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,710
Nice to meet you, Susan.

28
00:02:00,710 --> 00:02:02,610
Sorry I'm late.

29
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:08,530
The traffic. The parking. I was lost.

30
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,440
What pretty flowers! Thank you.

31
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:13,110
Oh, please come in.

32
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:16,460
Don't worry about being late. It's fine.

33
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:20,020
Excuse the mess. I just moved here.

34
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:23,070
Oh, I'd like you to meet my sister-in-law Marilyn.

35
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:25,510
Marilyn Stewart, this is Harry Bennett.

36
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:26,350
Pleased to meet you.

37
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:28,260
Nice to meet you, Harry.

38
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:30,190
Are we too late for our dinner reservation?

39
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:32,400
No, the restaurant will hold our table.

40
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,470
I know the owner very well.

41
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:34,570
I eat there a lot.

42
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:36,350
Do you know the phone number of the restaurant?

43
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:38,230
I'd like to call home

44
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:39,530
and leave the number with the baby-sitter.

45
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:50,230
Sure. The number is... five five five...seventeen twenty.

46
00:02:50,230 --> 00:03:01,670
May I use the phone?

47
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:07,140
Five five five...one seven two oh. Hello?

48
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,370
Hi, Michelle. It's Daddy.

49
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:10,820
Can I speak to Betty?

50
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:14,940
I want to leave the phone number of the restaurant...

51
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:19,910
Hi, Betty. I'll be at five five five...seventeen twenty.

52
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:24,720
OK. Thanks. See you later.

53
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:27,230
Well, that's done. Shall we go?

54
00:03:27,230 --> 00:03:29,450
I'm ready. See you later, Marilyn.

55
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,210
Have a nice evening.

56
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,900
Bye, Marilyn. Hope to see you again.

57
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,180
Me, too. Have fun!

58
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:39,610
Thanks.

59
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:42,610
After you.
